      "text": "Unity House opened in 1919 as a workers' utopia founded by Russian socialist garment organizers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://unityhouselives.com/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "For most of the 20th century, Unity House was a center for union organizing, lectures, and recreation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
